     "result_text_tail": "navy` theme; storyline approved as drafted.\n- **$0.6M running cost:** counted as a cost of revenue, the conservative choice for the margin figures.\n- **Churned accounts:** assumed to be average-sized, which is how the $1.1M at risk is sized.\n- **That $1.1M is a ceiling:** it assumes the rewrite would remove all mobile-related churn.\n- **Rewrite timing:** the 14 Copilot engineers go back to the mobile rewrite in Q3 2027.\n- **Pro take-up:** based on the 2023 tier launch. It's the weakest assumption behind the $2.9M, so the next steps include testing Pro pricing with accounts that weren't in the beta.\n- **850-request cap:** I worked it out from the 75% margin floor; it is not in the briefing pack.\n\n**Numbers:** 98 in total. 54 are taken directly from the pack with a word-for-word quote. 26 are simple calculations from those inputs. 18 are our own estimates, each with its formula shown on the slide and listed in the workbook with its assumptions. The workbook's Calculations sheet holds live Excel formulas, so changing an input updates the results.\n\nThe most useful next step is the Q4 2026 win rate against Routewise. It shows how much of the drop is AI rather than the promotion, which bears directly on whether launching in Q2 is worth the mobile delay. I can also switch the theme or add a backup slide that lists the assumptions.\n\nFiles are in `./deliverable/`:\n- dispatch-copilot.pptx\n- dispatch-copilot-sources.xlsx\n- dispatch-copilot.json (the spec, so the deck can be re-rendered)"
